+++ b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
@@ -159,8 +159,8 @@ Some features are not supported in AdvCiv-SAS; e.g., non-English languages, pre-
 - Consolidated **long, unneeded, or unused comments** into [Long_Comments/](/Long_Comments/) and replaced them with short custom markers or files to keep code clean, lean, and readable. > ~500k characters reduced and still ongoing.
 - **BBAI logging is now XML-tunable:** BBAI AI-decision logging can now be enabled/disabled and adjusted through **SAS defines**, rather than editing and recompiling the DLL as in base AdvCiv. This is deemed valuable **not only for modders, but also for users** who can now view or generate `BBAI.log` files for review. Note: `LoggingEnabled=1` in `CivilizationIV.ini` is still required for Civ4 to write. This allowed for example to surgically identify and fix the root cause of a city not producing its first settler until ~T90 at normal game speed, which is way too late (`bWarPlan` was too aggressively gating settler production; now it only blocks settler production after early expansion has reached enough cities (inefficient at that point, better switch strategy)). Note: BBAI logs can be very long; for broad raw-log diagnosis, we usually give to an external LLM/AI such as ChatGPT the log file, as it is as of now agentic-token-free analysis (also good to give us a different point of view/review if needed).
 - **Timestamped BBAI log files:** Optionally log each new game and loaded save to a **new UTC-timestamped file** (e.g., `BBAI_20260705T071718Z_new1.log` or `BBAI_20260705T071718Z_load2.log`) instead of expanding the existing `BBAI.log`, which was very tedious to clean up or identify/store/read/review/upload, and so repeated save-file tests no longer require restarting Civ4. Each log begins notably with the new/load time, currently active BBAI log levels, turn/year, map and game settings (including `landheavy` and `navalheavy` actual game information), player counts, and RNG states, avoiding mixed logs and the need to restart Civ4 between repeated save-file tests. See also [README.md (BBAI logging and head example)](/README.md#bbai-logging-and-head-example).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6022+) **SAS game-summary log:** added a separate `SASGameSummary_*.log` for compact autoplay and AI-strength review. It notably records high-level run context such as economy, expansion, city and battle history, worked plots, diplomacy, unit composition, game state, and in-game bonus appearances/disappearances, complementing BBAI logs by summarizing what happened before or alongside detailed AI-decision traces. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6033+) It also logs autoplay start/end/change rows, explicit player appearance/revival/elimination rows, and compact run-status rows with alive/eliminated players, current winner/victory if any, and top score/power players, so stopped autoplay logs no longer require inferring these from missing snapshots. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6034+) Free-text fields such as city, player, leader, civ, map-script, and log-file names are quoted/escaped, so names with spaces are easier to parse robustly. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6057+) It also notably records compact per-turn exploration, map changes and environmental status, explicit spaceship launches and project-victory progress, and a full final snapshot when the game is won. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6058+) It notably also records war-declaration causes and sponsors, diplomacy memories, progress for all enabled victories, project-victory resets and failures, and compact full-map revelation.
-- Note: it currently contains spoilers: a spoiler-free implementation was considered, so the human/active player can give to an LLM or such their play summary and get LLM or such suggestions or feedback/analysis, but it would require an extensive rework, so currently this is not supported; therefore, SAS game-summary log should as of now not be treated as a spoiler-free player-advice export. Note 2: depending on `SAS_GAME_SUMMARY_TURN_INTERVAL` value, the last turn may not appear in the log: for example, an autoplay run of 200 turns ends at T200 and thus does not seem to show the T200 data, only up to T190, so autoplay at least 201 turns to show T200 for example if you have this issue. For stronger LLM analysis, also provide compact mod context when possible; for example, the AdvCiv-SAS light source ZIP from [`make_light_source_zip.py`](/LLM_Helpers/README.md#make_light_source_zippy) includes useful source/XML/docs/helper context while staying compact enough to upload and share. See also [README.md (DLL Logging)](/README.md#dll-logging).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6022+) **SAS game-summary log:** added a separate `SASGameSummary_*.log` for compact autoplay and AI-strength review. It notably records high-level run context such as economy, expansion, city and battle history, worked plots, diplomacy, unit composition, game state, and in-game bonus appearances/disappearances, complementing BBAI logs by summarizing what happened before or alongside detailed AI-decision traces. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6033+) It also logs autoplay start/end/change rows, explicit player appearance/revival/elimination rows, and compact run-status rows with alive/eliminated players, current winner/victory if any, and top score/power players, so stopped autoplay logs no longer require inferring these from missing snapshots. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6034+) Free-text fields such as city, player, leader, civ, map-script, and log-file names are quoted/escaped, so names with spaces are easier to parse robustly. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6057+) It also notably records compact per-turn exploration, map changes and environmental status, explicit spaceship launches and project-victory progress, and a full final snapshot when the game is won. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6058+) It notably also records war-declaration causes and sponsors, diplomacy memories, progress for all enabled victories, project-victory resets and failures, and compact full-map revelation. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 6077+) It notably also further records active mod and DLL-slot identity, research and production overflow, production conversion and lost-production gold, city buildings and pollution, trade unlocks, and compact territory development including routes, improvements, irrigation, and improved/unimproved bonus types, and also names player-wide health/happiness modifier sources and records AI victory-stage strategies and the target's victory context when war is declared.
